# Testing Conventions

## Per-resource minimum

| Layer | Class | Approach |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Controller | `{Entity}ControllerTests` | `@WebMvcTest` + MockMvc |
| Service | `{Entity}ServiceTests` | JUnit 5 + `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` |
| Manual smoke | `api-testing/{resource}.http` | Ad-hoc REST Client requests to verify endpoints work (not part of the automated test suite) |

## Controller tests (Spring Boot 4)

Requires `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test` dependency.

```java
@WebMvcTest(UserController.class)
@Import(GlobalExceptionHandler.class)
class UserControllerTests {
    @Autowired MockMvc mockMvc;
    @MockitoBean UserService userService;
}
```

- Import `GlobalExceptionHandler` to assert error envelopes
- Mock the service, not the repository
- Assert DTO JSON shapes (`UserResponse`, `MobilePrefixSearchResponse`)

## Service tests

- `@Mock` repository, `@InjectMocks` service — no Spring context
- Test `ResourceNotFoundException`, `IllegalArgumentException`, and DTO mapping behavior

## Manual `.http` files (`api-testing/`)

Not an automated testing module — optional REST Client files for manually hitting endpoints during development.

- Variables at top: `@baseUrl`, resource ids
- Include POST, PUT, GET, DELETE, and expected 400/404 cases
- Match current DTO request/response shapes
- Use anonymized placeholder data only

## SQL integration tests

Not used yet. When added, prefer **Testcontainers + PostgreSQL** over H2 for PG-specific SQL.
